{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"]]},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"title":"How-to Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill"],"anchor":"How-to-Guides","generated":true}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddPersistence"},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"metadata":{"title":"Add Persistence","modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddpersistence"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Persist your domain entities to SwiftData with the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" macro — no hand-written "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Model"},{"type":"text","text":" classes, database actors, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" turns persistence into a declare-and-register concern. You annotate a domain entity with "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; the macro generates its SwiftData "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" “shadow” class, the value↔model converters, and the "},{"code":"PersistableEntity","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" conformance. A generic "},{"code":"EntityDB","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" actor and a "},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" build the container, synthesize one "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" per registered "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":", and reuse the core "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" for debounced, batched writes."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reducers mutate plain value-type entities inside an "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":"; the plugin observes the changelog and writes through to SwiftData after a debounce. Reads happen once, at launch, into memory — the in-memory "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" is the source of truth."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For low-level manual wiring (writing your own "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"@Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"), see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide"},{"type":"text","text":". For the macro details, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference"},{"type":"text","text":". To add cross-device iCloud sync on top, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Before you start","anchor":"Before-you-start"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This guide assumes a Swidux app already exists — "},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AppAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"AppReducer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"code":"AppStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are wired and the store is in the SwiftUI environment. If not, follow "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" first."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a local-only persistence layer. It needs "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no iCloud, CloudKit, or Push entitlements"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — only the sandbox "},{"code":"com.apple.security.network.client","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entitlement if your app also makes network calls (killswitch, analytics, feature flags). Adding sync entitlements to a local-only app is dead configuration and an App Review risk."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 1: Add the dependency","anchor":"Step-1-Add-the-dependency"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add the "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" product to your app target in "},{"code":"Package.swift","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":[".target(","    name: \"MyApp\",","    dependencies: [","        \"Swidux\",","        \"SwiduxPersistence\",","    ]",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 2: Annotate your domain entity with `@Persisted`","anchor":"Step-2-Annotate-your-domain-entity-with-Persisted"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A persisted entity is a value type that already satisfies "},{"code":"Identifiable & Equatable & Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"ID == UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" contract). Add "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","    var createdAt: Date","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This generates a "},{"code":"CardModel: @Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" class with "},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"toDomain()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"update(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", plus "},{"code":"extension Card: PersistableEntity { typealias Model = CardModel }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". By default every stored property is mirrored directly onto the model — SwiftData persists scalars "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" composites natively, so no manual blob columns are needed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated model is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"CloudKit-safe by construction"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"same"}]},{"type":"text","text":" model backs both the local and the synced container (see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync"},{"type":"text","text":"). SwiftData’s CloudKit mirroring requires every non-optional attribute to be optional or carry a default value, and every relationship to be optional — validated when the "},{"code":"ModelContainer","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is created. "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" satisfies this automatically:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Non-optional mirrored attributes get a default.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" If you wrote one on the domain property ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var count: Int = 0"},{"type":"text","text":"), it is propagated verbatim; otherwise the macro fills a canonical default for the known SwiftData primitives ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String → \"\""},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Bool → false"},{"type":"text","text":", integers\/floats "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"→ 0"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Date → .distantPast"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data → Data()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UUID → UUID()"},{"type":"text","text":"). Defaults are inert locally — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" overwrites them on every load."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Non-primitive, non-optional properties","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (a custom "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" type, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URL"},{"type":"text","text":", an enum) have no default the macro can invent. Give the property a default ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"= …"},{"type":"text","text":"), make it optional, or mark it "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"type":"text","text":" — otherwise "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" emits a compile-time error."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Relationships are generated optional","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"var tags: [TagModel]? = nil"},{"type":"text","text":"); a non-optional to-one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relation"},{"type":"text","text":" is a compile-time error (CloudKit forbids non-optional relationships)."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"text":" blob columns","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" default to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data()"},{"type":"text","text":", so any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" type is CloudKit-safe through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"type":"text","text":". Because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data()"},{"type":"text","text":" is never decodable, a "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"non-optional","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Inline"},{"type":"text","text":" property must also carry a domain default ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"= …"},{"type":"text","text":") — the generated getter falls back to it when the blob is missing or undecodable (e.g. a row CloudKit materialized before the blob synced). Omitting the default is a compile-time error ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inlineRequiresDefault"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"entity"}]},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" lives on "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"state containers"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":"AppState","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" slices). They are different layers and never apply to the same type."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Marker macros for non-trivial properties","anchor":"Marker-macros-for-non-trivial-properties"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A macro can’t infer relationships, foreign keys, or which fields are derived. Four property markers (named to avoid SwiftData’s own "},{"code":"@Relationship","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"code":"@Transient","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") tell "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" what to do:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@Persisted","nonisolated struct Card: Identifiable, Equatable, Sendable {","    var id: UUID","    var quote: String","","    @Inline var styling: TextStyling = TextStyling()  \/\/ one opaque JSON Data column","    @ForeignKey var deckID: UUID                      \/\/ scalar parent reference","    @Relation(deleteRule: .cascade, inverse: \\TagModel.card)","    var tags: [Tag]                                   \/\/ SwiftData relationship","    @Ignored var renderedPreview: String?             \/\/ derived; omitted from the model","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Marker"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Effect"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"(none)"}],"type":"emphasis"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Mirror the property directly (SwiftData persists scalars and "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" composites)."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Inline","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Force a "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" value into a single JSON "},{"code":"Data","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" column (keeps a CloudKit record compact; sidesteps SwiftData "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"-attribute edge cases)."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@ForeignKey","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Intent marker on a "},{"code":"UUID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; functionally a mirrored scalar column."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Relation(deleteRule:inverse:)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A SwiftData relationship to another "},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" entity. The property’s type references the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"domain"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" type ("},{"code":"[Tag]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Tag?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"Tag","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); the model substitutes the "},{"code":"…Model","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" shadow. "},{"code":"inverse","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a key path on the generated model, e.g. "},{"code":"\\TagModel.card","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"code":"deleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"code":"SwiduxDeleteRule","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"code":".cascade","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".nullify","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".noAction","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":".deny","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Ignored","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Exclude a derived\/denormalized property. Must be optional so it can be reconstructed as "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on load."}]}]]]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"code":"@Persisted","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" does not generate an "},{"code":"@Attribute(.unique)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — CloudKit forbids unique constraints — so the same generated model works for both local and synced containers. The cost is that rows sharing an "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are possible. "},{"code":"EntityDB","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handles them by converging rather than by assuming uniqueness: writes update every matching row, deletions remove every matching row, and "},{"code":"fetchAll","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" collapses to one value per "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Nothing deletes a duplicate as a side effect of a write."}]}],"style":"note","name":"Note"},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 3: Put the `EntityStore` on your state","anchor":"Step-3-Put-the-EntityStore-on-your-state"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@Swidux","nonisolated struct AppState: Equatable, Sendable {","    var cards: EntityStore<Card> = .init()","    \/\/ ... your other slices","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Your reducers mutate "},{"code":"state.cards","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" like any "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"code":"state.cards[card.id] = card","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"state.cards.modify(id) { … }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"state.cards[id] = nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Every change is recorded for the plugin to drain."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Step 4: Build the coordinator and register the plugin","anchor":"Step-4-Build-the-coordinator-and-register-the-plugin"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In "},{"code":"Store.configured()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", build a local container, create a "},{"code":"PersistenceCoordinator","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", register its plugin, and run first-load hydration before constructing the store:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["import SwiduxPersistence","","extension Store where State == AppState, Action == AppAction {","    static func configured() async -> AppStore {","        let container = try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","","        let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","            entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","            container: container,","            debounce: .milliseconds(250)","        )","","        let plugins = PluginHost<AppState, AppAction>()","        \/\/ Register UndoPlugin first if you use it — snapshots must precede writes.","        plugins.register(persistence.corePlugin)","","        var initial = AppState()","        await persistence.hydrate(into: &initial)   \/\/ first-load: fill EntityStores from disk","","        return Store(initialState: initial, reducer: { … }, plugins: plugins)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"hydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"first-load only"}]},{"type":"text","text":" — it replaces each "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore"},{"type":"text","text":" with the on-disk rows before any live edits exist. It takes "},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" because it runs "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before the store is built"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so there is nothing to race with."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The only refresh path after launch is "},{"code":"rehydrate(into:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"reconciles"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rather than replaces: rows on disk are authoritative except for IDs that still carry unflushed local intent, which always win. So a “refresh from disk” can never clobber pending writes or in-progress UI edits, while remote edits and deletions still surface mid-session. Pass "},{"code":"policy:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — or register an entity with "},{"code":"policy:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — to narrow that; see "},{"code":"MergePolicy","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It takes the "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"store"}]},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":": re-hydration is asynchronous, and a caller holding a state snapshot across those "},{"code":"await","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s would discard everything dispatched while they were in flight. See "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting"},{"type":"text","text":" if edits are vanishing after a load."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you need to "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"read"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rows without touching state, don’t re-hydrate into a throwaway "},{"code":"AppState()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — that idiom breaks silently the moment re-hydration starts reading the state it is handed. Use "},{"code":"fetchAll(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" \/ "},{"code":"snapshot(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on the coordinator instead."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Reading rows without touching state","anchor":"Reading-rows-without-touching-state"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For exports, migrations, diagnostics, or any other “what’s actually on disk?” question, read directly — naming your domain type, not its generated shadow:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let notes = try await persistence.fetchAll(of: Note.self)","let store = try await persistence.snapshot(of: Note.self)   \/\/ as an EntityStore"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Both flush the debounce window first by default, so they can’t return a stale row for something the user just edited; pass "},{"code":"flushPending: false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on a hot path where that doesn’t matter. Both report failures to "},{"code":"onFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rethrow — there is no state to leave untouched here, so swallowing the error could only present an unreadable database as “no data”."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The entity does not have to be registered with the coordinator; reading a model that is in the container’s schema but not mirrored into state is fine."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Don’t answer these questions by re-hydrating into a throwaway "},{"code":"AppState()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". That reads like a pure fetch but is really a merge, and it breaks silently the moment re-hydration starts consulting the state it is handed."}]}],"style":"important","name":"Important"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Surfacing failures","anchor":"Surfacing-failures"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every save and fetch failure is logged, and the coordinator accepts an optional "},{"code":"onFailure:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" handler to additionally surface it to your app (a failed "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"save"}]},{"type":"text","text":" means the in-memory data is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}]},{"type":"text","text":" on disk; a failed "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"hydrate fetch"}]},{"type":"text","text":" leaves that "},{"code":"EntityStore","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" untouched rather than presenting an unreadable store as “no data”):"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","    container: container,","    onFailure: { failure in","        guard failure.isFinal else { return }   \/\/ earlier attempts may still succeed","        \/\/ e.g. dispatch an action that shows a \"couldn't save\" banner","    }",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"level":3,"anchor":"Retrying-a-failed-save","type":"heading","text":"Retrying a failed save"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A flush clears its buffers before the save runs, so a save that fails has nothing left to retry it — the write would reach disk only if the user happened to touch the same entity again. That is silent data loss, so the stack retries."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A failed batch goes "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"back","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" into the writer’s pending buffers, never over anything newer: a later edit to the same entity supersedes the restored value, and a deletion drained while the save was in flight cancels it. "},{"code":"PersistencePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" then re-attempts on a doubling backoff, independently of the debounce timer — a write has to land even if the user never touches the app again."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Retrying is bounded, because a write that can "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"never"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" succeed (disk full, a model the container can’t encode) must not keep the stack busy forever. Tune it with "},{"code":"retry:","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.cards)],","    container: container,","    retry: RetryPolicy(maxAttempts: 5, baseDelay: .milliseconds(500), maxDelay: .seconds(30)),","    onFailure: { failure in ... }",")"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"RetryPolicy.default","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is that policy — five attempts over roughly seven seconds. "},{"code":"RetryPolicy.never","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" opts out of retrying without opting back into losing the write."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When the budget runs out you get one final "},{"code":"PersistenceFailure","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"code":"isFinal == true","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". That is the one worth telling the user about: everything before it was “we’ll try again”. The batch is "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"not"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" discarded — it stays pending, so the next edit or an explicit "},{"code":"flush()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tries once more, and until then those IDs stay locally owned so a re-hydration can’t overwrite them with the stale stored row."}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every attempt is reported, so a handler that shows UI should gate on "},{"code":"isFinal","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Most "},{"code":".save","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" failures are transient and are followed by a success the app never hears about."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"note","name":"Note"},{"text":"Diagnostics: what isn’t a failure","type":"heading","anchor":"Diagnostics-what-isnt-a-failure","level":3},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some conditions are worth acting on but aren’t errors, so routing them through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onFailure"},{"type":"text","text":" would be wrong. Duplicate rows are the clearest case: CloudKit forbids unique constraints, so several rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" are a legitimate on-disk state, not a fault. They go to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"onDiagnostic:"},{"type":"text","text":" instead:"}]},{"code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.cards, collapse: EntityCollapse.byID { $0.updatedAt >= $1.updatedAt ? $0 : $1 })],","    container: container,","    onDiagnostic: { diagnostic in","        guard diagnostic.kind == .duplicateRowsCollapsed,","              let count = diagnostic.duplicateCount else { return }","        store.send(.offerDuplicateCleanup(count: count))","    }",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Three kinds ship today:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Kind"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Means"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Payload"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".duplicateRowsCollapsed"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A read found rows sharing an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":". Without a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"collapse:"},{"type":"text","text":" resolver they are harmless but permanent — this is what lets you "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"offer"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the cleanup."}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entityType"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"duplicateCount"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".possibleDispatchLoop"}]}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" fired far more often in one debounce interval than a user could cause. Usually an effect or plugin dispatching on every state change. Reported once per burst, not once per dispatch."}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"drainCount","type":"codeVoice"}]}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".writesUnpersisted"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The set of IDs whose last flush failed changed. Fires again with an "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"empty"}]},{"type":"text","text":" set once they land, so an indicator can be cleared rather than guessed at."}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"entityType"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unpersistedIDs"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceDiagnostic"},{"text":" is a struct with static constructors rather than an enum, so a future kind can’t break an exhaustive ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"text":" in your code — match on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"kind"},{"text":" and read the payload you expect. Duplicate reads and dispatch loops are logged whether or not you supply a handler; the unpersisted set has no log of its own, because the individual ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PersistenceFailure"},{"type":"text","text":"s behind it are already logged."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Step-5-Flush-on-background","type":"heading","text":"Step 5: Flush on background"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Writes are debounced, so drain them when the app is backgrounded or terminates:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":[".onChange(of: scenePhase) { _, phase in","    if phase == .background {","        Task { await persistence.corePlugin.flush() }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"text":"Multiple entities and ordering","level":2,"anchor":"Multiple-entities-and-ordering","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Register one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".entity(\\.keyPath)"},{"type":"text","text":" per "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let persistence = PersistenceCoordinator<AppState, AppAction>(","    entities: [.entity(\\.decks), .entity(\\.cards), .entity(\\.tags)],","    container: try! ContainerFactory.makeLocalContainer(","        models: [DeckModel.self, CardModel.self, TagModel.self]","    )",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass every generated "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"…Model"},{"type":"text","text":" type to the container’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"models:"},{"type":"text","text":". Writers flush in registration order — if entity B holds a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Relation"},{"type":"text","text":" to A, register A’s entity first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"anchor":"Testing","type":"heading","text":"Testing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The whole stack runs against an in-memory SwiftData store, so persistence is unit-testable with no disk and no CloudKit:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let container = try ContainerFactory.makeInMemoryContainer(models: [CardModel.self])","let db = EntityDB(modelContainer: container)","","try await db.upsert(Card(id: id, quote: \"hi\", createdAt: .now), as: CardModel.self)","let all = try await db.fetchAll(CardModel.self)","#expect(all.first?.quote == \"hi\")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To prove the rule-#8 merge guarantee, seed the store, make a live in-memory edit, call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"coordinator.rehydrate(into:)"},{"text":", and assert the live edit survives.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Troubleshooting":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Troubleshooting","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/troubleshooting","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Symptoms you may hit while adopting Swidux, and what each one actually means."}],"kind":"article","title":"Troubleshooting"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch":{"title":"Add a Version Killswitch","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAVersionKillswitch","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire a remote-controlled blocker that prevents unsupported app versions from running, with an “Update” path back to the App Store."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaversionkillswitch","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingADomainPlugin":{"title":"Building a Domain Plugin","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Create a self-contained feature plugin with its own state, actions, and effects.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingADomainPlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingadomainplugin","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/MacrosReference":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/MacrosReference","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/macrosreference","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Reference for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Slice"},{"type":"text","text":" (the observation bridge between value-type state and SwiftUI), and for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Persisted"},{"type":"text","text":" and its property markers (the SwiftData persistence bridge, shipped in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxPersistence"},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"kind":"article","title":"Macros"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"PersistencePlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAnalytics":{"title":"Add Analytics","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxAnalytics","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for centralized event tracking with declarative event mapping and auto-identify."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAnalytics","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddanalytics","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddFeatureFlags":{"title":"Add Feature Flags","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddFeatureFlags","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxFeatureFlags"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app for typed feature flags, A\/B variants, and remote-tunable scalar values from a single JSON config."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddfeatureflags","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/GettingStarted":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/GettingStarted","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/gettingstarted","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Swidux to your project and wire up unidirectional data flow with automatic persistence."}],"kind":"article","title":"Getting Started with Swidux"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/AgentSkill":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/AgentSkill","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/agentskill","title":"Using the Swidux Agent Skill","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Install the bundled "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"swidux-ref"},{"type":"text","text":" skill so your AI coding assistant has Swidux’s architecture rules and code templates on hand."}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddICloudSync":{"title":"Add iCloud Sync","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Layer opt-in, cross-device iCloud sync on top of "},{"code":"SwiduxPersistence","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" with the "},{"code":"SwiduxCloudKitSync","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin — including a runtime opt-out toggle, launch-time entitlement detection, and the Apple Developer portal configuration."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddICloudSync","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddicloudsync","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistenceMiddlewareGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistencemiddlewareguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Configure automatic persistence that drains entity changes and batches database writes."}],"kind":"article","title":"Persistence Middleware"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAParentalGate":{"title":"Add a Parental Gate","role":"article","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gate sensitive actions — purchases, settings changes, leaving a kid-mode area — behind a math challenge."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAParentalGate","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddaparentalgate","kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"title":"Swidux","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","role":"collection"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"kind":"symbol","title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStoreGuide":{"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStoreGuide","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystoreguide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection with built-in change tracking."}],"kind":"article","title":"EntityStore"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToAddAPaywall":{"title":"Add a Paywall","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToAddAPaywall","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Wire the "},{"code":"SwiduxPaywall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" plugin into a Swidux app to gate features behind a subscription or lifetime purchase."}],"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtoaddapaywall","role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/HowToCancelEffects":{"title":"Cancel Effects","role":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tag an effect with an identity so it can be cancelled later — by another effect, or imperatively from view code."}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/HowToCancelEffects","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/howtocanceleffects","kind":"article"}}}